<h2>Three changes, none needing new configuration</h2>
<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Changes in this release">
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Change</th><th scope="col">What you get</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row"><code>--env-file PATH</code></th><td data-label="What you get">The daemon reads literal <code>KEY=VALUE</code> lines before serving; a command-line option or inherited variable wins over the file. It refuses a file that isn't private to the daemon's user, and its errors never print a key or value. <a href="{{ source }}/docs/gatewayd.md#environment-file">File rules ↗</a></td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Quiet reload polls</th><td data-label="What you get">A reload poll that finds nothing changed answers without rebuilding the broker or its Cedar policy, so an idle broker stays idle.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Wasmtime advisories</th><td data-label="What you get">Both Wasmtime builds take the fix for RUSTSEC-2026-0422, RUSTSEC-2026-0423 and RUSTSEC-2026-0424.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="limits"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-scope-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>An env file keeps its secrets in plain text</h2>
<p>The file holds literal values on disk, and anything running as that daemon's user can read it. Keep provider credentials in the broker's credential file: the broker reads none from its environment.</p>
</section>

